## How to use this file

This file is the project's **constitution** — stable architectural facts, conventions, and constraints. Read it first, every session.

For volatile state (what we did yesterday, current bugs, in-flight work), see [HANDOVER.md](./HANDOVER.md).

---

## Reading order (for AI sessions)

Don't load the whole project into context. Read only what your task needs:

| What you're doing | What to read (in order) |
|---|---|
| Modifying a single module | This file → `path/to/module/` → its tests |
| Adding a new feature | This file → relevant ADR → existing similar feature as template |
| Debugging a failure | This file → HANDOVER.md ⚠️ traps section → reproduce → instrument |
| Onboarding (first time) | This file → README.md → one example feature end-to-end |
| Modifying architecture | **Stop and ask the human first** — this is a design decision |

**Rule**: load the smallest set you think you need. Add more only when you discover a gap. Don't pre-load "just in case."

